    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2PuuZ57ZHgtnWZ2CokA3sJZ)_\n\n## What\n- New option `sp-batch-report-save-and-kill` (default `t`) in `sp-batch-report`; set it to `nil` to get each command's old rule back.\n- Three helpers, with no prompts and no messages (`inhibit-message`, `save-silently`, short answers, no kill query, no \"changed on disk\" question):\n  - `sp-batch-report-flush-file FILE [BACKUP]`: saves an open buffer with unsaved changes (after `BACKUP` copied the disk text), reverts a stale unchanged one.\n  - `sp-batch-report-close-file FILE`: saves, then kills the buffer.\n  - `sp-batch-report-with-file FILE FN [BACKUP]`: flush, run in the buffer, close.\n- Edge cases:\n  - Unsaved changes are saved; the backup keeps the disk text first (the titles and meta backups now keep the first copy of a run instead of failing on a second one).\n  - File changed on disk and edited in the buffer: the buffer wins.\n  - The buffer you are in (current, or in the selected window, or bound in `sp-batch-report-keep-buffers`) is saved but not killed. The Works command of an author note binds it, since it runs from the note.\n  - A buffer that cannot be saved is not killed; a failed kill is only written to `*Messages*`.\n  - Files locked by another Emacs are still skipped by the titles command.\n- Used by: author notes passes (`sp-author-notes--process-file`, `--populate`), `sp-litnotes-refs`, `sp-litnotes-titles`, and `sp-litnotes-meta` (status, parent lint, title lint, chapter tables).\n- Not changed: `sp-bibprocess` (BibTeX files), `sp-see-also`, `sp-notes`, and the interactive single-note commands of `sp-litnotes-meta`.\n- Note: `sp-batch-process` does not exist; the helpers live in `sp-batch-report`.\n- Docs: `docs/tangles/funct/sp-batch-report.org` has a bullet section and a changes entry; the tangle check passes.\n\n## Tests\n- 9 new ERT tests in `sp-batch-report-test.el` (17 pass), 2 in `sp-litnotes-meta-test.el` (68 pass), 1 new and 1 renamed in `sp-litnotes-titles-test.el`. Author notes (36) and refs (7) pass.\n- `sp-litnotes-titles-bib-authors-surname` fails here with or without this change (`sp-author-notes-latex-to-unicode` is not loaded in that test).\n\n## Manual testing\n- [ ] `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 425-quiet-batch-buffers; git checkout 425-quiet-batch-buffers`, restart Emacs.\n- [ ] Unit tests: `cd ~/.config/emacs-modular; for t in batch-report author-notes litnotes-refs litnotes-meta; do emacs -Q --batch -L libraries/modules/funct -L libraries/modules/academic -L libraries/modules/vulpea -l ert -l tests/sp-$t-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit; done` → 17, 36, 7, 68 pass.\n- [ ] Unsaved edit: open a litnote, type a character without saving, run `M-x sp-litnotes-titles-dryrun` then the convert on it (pick one note) → no question, the note is saved and its buffer gone (`C-x b` no longer lists it); the backup folder has the text from before. (untested by Claude on the real vault)\n- [ ] Run `M-x sp-author-notes-works-convert` (or the author notes convert) in a note: the note you are in stays open and saved; other notes it touched are closed, with no prompts. (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] File changed on disk while its buffer has edits (edit the file in a shell, then type in the buffer), run a batch command on it → saved without the \"changed on disk\" question; the disk text is in the backup.\n- [ ] Edge: `(setq sp-batch-report-save-and-kill nil)`, repeat the unsaved-edit step → the note is skipped or refused as before.\n- [ ] Regression: `M-x sp-litnotes-meta-refresh-all-tables` and the status report (`sp-litnotes-meta-set-status`) still work; `C-u` previews write nothing.\n- [ ] Not changed: BibTeX lint (`sp-bibprocess`) still asks as before.\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard any local edits made while testing: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .` (and `git clean -fd` only after checking `git clean -nd`).\n- Return to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main` and `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`.\n- Optionally delete the test branch locally: `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D 425-quiet-batch-buffers`; the remote copy stays until the PR is merged or closed.\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`) so the config matches main again.\n- If a command changed the vault (litnotes), restore from the backup folder the command reported, or `git -C ~/notes restore .` if the vault is under git.\n- Fish shell works for all of the above; Sia uses GNU Stow, so no yadm steps.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9yt8Zs5BRFNz7Hfuz)_",
